bc.com","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":4},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"46ff41c8d73eeba87776635ef3d579b523f33ee9eb6617e2ab03bd3b58ef5727","event_uuid":"6950dd58-19a6-4e4e-afd2-f553ee3cd58c","position":{"commit_sha":"688f87f60d7ff9805e0576bfd9d695d641e2cc07","position":"1786760472850008001-6950dd58-19a6-4e4e-afd2-f553ee3cd58c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1cb047ec259bd6158746281311e3195fd1899d9c9dfec73d5bf9ce816a612a45","event_uuid":"667d6ea1-f528-4f10-acb0-3184618e2af2","position":{"commit_sha":"88f7f699855968e7391a878175958227e48aec51","position":"1786761469114658001-667d6ea1-f528-4f10-acb0-3184618e2af2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c6bb1d8e83cb8ab130c7aae9ce52d64eb34f356071f73e82e6233fd18a5cb1bc","event_uuid":"6db66459-47a6-4c8b-8552-2036397abc45","position":{"commit_sha":"29b1cf7bfc5e687fcdf7a30773d7ef2e6456dfc5","position":"1786761528665618001-6db66459-47a6-4c8b-8552-2036397abc45"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bfd92faedbc019433841f776839f7e4f7cd24edffa23b872eb7f4478021abb13","event_uuid":"8d126a4e-d266-42d3-9002-273483ffc528","position":{"commit_sha":"9fb5935773deaade2d1318beed2fd342d2bd6b55","position":"1786762997336640001-8d126a4e-d266-42d3-9002-273483ffc528"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Organic control captured from unrelated Gerrit change 1801 patchset 1 (commit 8869710; run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31859036505). The workflow-dispatch run started 2026-08-15T02:22:55Z and cast Verified at 02:44:43Z: 21m48s end-to-end, success. The macOS job became active at 02:24:21Z (86s after dispatch), began pytest at 02:24:59Z after checkout/setup/gates, and completed at 02:44:30Z: 20m09s job wall time. macOS default was 13,393 passed / 65 skipped in 1,017.42s (16m57s); integration was 158 passed / 11 skipped in 98.71s (1m38s). No macOS phase exceeded 20s: the slowest default call was show-under-write-burst at 13.15s; the import benchmark led integration at 19.69s; partial-clone fixture setups were 9.03-9.08s. Ubuntu 3.11 job/default/integration: 9m32s / 7m07s / 1m19s (13,394 passed, 64 skipped; 158 passed, 11 skipped). Ubuntu 3.12: 9m48s / 7m21s / 1m24s. Ubuntu 3.13 with coverage: 12m44s / 10m22s / 1m20s. Import benchmark calls were 15.76s, 14.72s, and 15.76s respectively. This is the no-extra-run control required by AC1. Retention oracle for the experiment: the RAM-disk macOS job/default must improve by at least the larger of 5% or the observed recent-green range versus this control and the 24m42s/21m11s post-DNS run; Ubuntu must stay within its observed range.","timestamp":1786762997336640001}],"created_at":1786759962363224001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"025527d7-712c-454e-b0ef-f90adef11e58","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"41d2-2814-a368-4c79"},{"link_uuid":"7a861799-26fe-4f78-8ff0-5c7a2feba5c8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c5be-ce38-60a6-47ea"}],"description":"## Context and evidence\n\nThe remaining macOS critical path is filesystem-heavy. The N=3000 import long pole reproduces at 20.19-21.63s on the same macOS host with 15.39-16.65s system CPU versus 4.59-5.67s user CPU. cProfile attributes 13.69s to 24 required git-add/git-commit pairs, while the full default suite creates thousands of temporary Git stores below pytest --basetemp. The workflow deliberately uses runner.temp rather than /tmp because the macOS tmp cleaner previously deleted live test trees.\n\nMaintained OSS precedent matches this mechanism. Apple Git CI creates a 4GB APFS RAM disk for test output and documents greater-than-2x test speedup from avoiding slow storage for many small writes (apple-oss-distributions/Git src/git/.gitlab-ci.yml lines 82-88 at 6b2f9bfe). Aeron creates a macOS APFS RAM disk in GitHub Actions for its temporary test filesystem (aeron-io/aeron .github/workflows/ci.yml lines 62-68 at 092f184a). Git t/perf/README says putting test roots on tmpfs can massively speed the suite. Tracker search found no prior RAM-disk/tmpfs proposal or rejection. This changes storage placement only: no test, worker, platform, behavioral assertion, coverage, mutation work, or runner is removed or added.\n\nOperator direction: do not land a control-only patchset, because an extra full-matrix run would create the contention this work is intended to reduce. Use the next full Verify run initiated by another session as the timing control. Storage sizing comes from the stable local full-suite temp tree or one local explicit-basetemp reproduction; only an implementation change may trigger another Gerrit run.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Watch the next unrelated full Gerrit Verify run. Capture its macOS default/integration/job and Ubuntu job wall times, slow-duration tail, queue delay, and run conclusion as the control without modifying that change.\n2. Measure retained temp allocated bytes and file count from a stable local full-suite run using the same selectors and distinct explicit basetemps. Size the RAM disk with at least 50% headroom while keeping it below 40% of detected runner physical memory. If the requirement cannot fit, stop and report infeasibility rather than risk memory pressure or a full volume.\n3. In the existing build/test matrix job, create an APFS RAM disk only when runner.os is macOS, after setup/gates and immediately before pytest. Publish its mount path through a step output; non-macOS cells continue using runner.temp byte-for-byte. Route both unchanged pytest selectors to separate basetemps below that mount.\n4. Always report filesystem type, allocated bytes, file count, and capacity, then detach the exact device created by setup after both pytest tiers, including failure/cancellation paths where GitHub permits cleanup. Do not use a broad disk target, persistent mount, cache, extra runner, or extra job.\n5. Add static workflow contract tests proving macOS-only creation, measured bounded sizing, unchanged selectors/xdist worker counts/timeouts/coverage flags, distinct default/integration basetemps, and always-run exact-device cleanup. Run actionlint and zizmor.\n6. Push the implementation through Gerrit immediately. Compare its macOS default/integration/job wall times with the unrelated control and recent post-DNS green runs; report absolute/percentage savings and Ubuntu non-regression. Retain it only if the full matrix is green and macOS runner time decreases beyond ordinary run variation.\n\n## Test contract card\n\nauthoritative_contract: .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml executes the unchanged default and integration pytest selectors on Ubuntu 3.11/3.12/3.13 and macOS 3.13, with coverage once on Ubuntu 3.13.\ntrigger_preconditions: macOS matrix cell reaches the pytest steps after all existing gates.\nproduction_path: GitHub Actions creates an ephemeral APFS RAM device, pytest tmp_path/basetemp writes real Git repositories there, then cleanup detaches only that device.\ntest_tier: static workflow contract tests plus the actual full Gerrit Verify matrix.\nobservable_postcondition: identical collection/pass/skip counts and gates, lower macOS pytest/job wall time, bounded RAM use, no mounted device after cleanup.\nnegative_control: every Ubuntu cell keeps runner.temp and existing behavior; a RAM-disk setup/sizing failure fails loudly before tests rather than silently changing coverage.\ncollateral_invariants: no test selection, assertion, marker, worker count, timeout, coverage, mutation shard, Python/platform cell, or runner concurrency changes.\nci_gate: actionlint, zizmor, workflow contract tests, full Gerrit Verify, LLM-Review.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The next unrelated full Verify run records control macOS default/integration/job wall times, Ubuntu job times, queue delay, slow tail, and conclusion without a control-only patchset.\n- [ ] Local retained-temp evidence yields at least 50% RAM-disk headroom below 40% of detected physical memory.\n- [ ] Only the macOS cell creates and uses the APFS RAM disk; all Ubuntu cells retain runner.temp.\n- [ ] Default and integration selectors, markers, xdist counts/distribution, timeouts, coverage-once behavior, collection/pass/skip counts, and all platform/Python cells remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Cleanup runs under always(), reports final filesystem usage, and detaches only the exact device created by setup.\n- [ ] Static workflow tests, actionlint, zizmor, focused/full pytest, LLM-Review, and Gerrit Verified are green.\n- [ ] Control-versus-RAM-disk evidence shows a macOS runner-time decrease beyond recent run variation with no Ubuntu regression; otherwise the experimental change is not retained.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"measure existing pytest temp usage, then create/use/clean a bounded macOS-only RAM disk without changing selectors"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_macos_ramdisk.py","reason":"pin macOS-only routing, bounded sizing, unchanged pytest contracts, and exact-device always cleanup"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","managed_refs":[["relates_to","c5be-ce38-60a6-47ea"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6db66459-47a6-4c8b-8552-2036397abc45","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","performance","macos","pytest"],"ticket_id":"9d44-c0c0-8d4d-4074","ticket_type":"task","title":"Use a measured macOS RAM disk for Git-heavy pytest temp trees","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["49995f90-45db-46e8-bd55-5cfb8de4b812","7dbaa1f3-1067-45a3-a1cb-ff2efff13d7e","025527d7-712c-454e-b0ef-f90adef11e58","7a861799-26fe-4f78-8ff0-5c7a2feba5c8","6950dd58-19a6-4e4e-afd2-f553ee3cd58c","667d6ea1-f528-4f10-acb0-3184618e2af2","6db66459-47a6-4c8b-8552-2036397abc45","8d126a4e-d266-42d3-9002-273483ffc528"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786772518602223001,"uuid":"6d341eac-a7ff-4573-8fef-2a2ab26a9ced"}